SYNTHESIS
  Incoming KPS S19 refutes the scalar C(k)=sup w|Delta_w| route.
  Therefore AP-triple packets are not being used to bound C(k).
  They are phase coordinates for the direct wide=>small-p0 coverage lemma.
  Rank-one relation u-2v+w=0 is preserved by every AP triple, but packet
  signs, pair-tax shadow, and Eisenstein imbalance vary with offset and core.
  A finite resonant atlas must retain this phase/support address before
  applying any signed relation-lattice or Freiman/GAP reduction.
  No LRC(14) proof is claimed.
